    {
      "key": "ScreenCapturer",
      "kind": "class",
      "doc": {
        "summary": "Asynchronously selects capture targets and obtains independent SDR images.",
        "details": "Calls use the host UI thread and require a running event loop. Completions run on a later UI-loop turn exactly once. Without a dispatcher, failure is delivered synchronously on the caller thread. An empty callback does nothing. Runtime shutdown can revoke pending deliveries. Queries never prompt for permission.\n\n```cpp\nauto source = CaptureSource::FromDisplay(DisplayManager::GetInstance().GetPrimary());\nScreenCapturer::Capture(source, {}, [](bool ok, std::shared_ptr<Image> image) {\n  if (ok) image->SaveToFile(\"/tmp/screenshot.png\");\n});\n```",
        "notes": [
          {
            "kind": "note",
            "text": "Platform availability:\n- macOS: ⚠️ ScreenCaptureKit on macOS 14+; selection uses the system sharing picker\n- Windows: ⚠️ Windows 10 2004+; picker needs an owner window and both source types enabled; system-selected sources have type Unknown\n- Linux: ❌ Not implemented - Queries return false and operations fail\n- Android: ❌ Not implemented - Queries return false and operations fail\n- iOS: ❌ Not implemented - Queries return false and operations fail\n- OpenHarmony: ❌ Not implemented - Queries return false and operations fail"
          }
        ]
      },
